Chapter: MutableThread
  cites Codex chapter General

 A mutable record is uniquely owned but may be read as often as you like.
 Reading a field is free; threading the record through a function that
 returns it (here `step`) consumes it once. Single-owner use is accepted.

Section: Definitions

  mutable Box = record {
    n : Integer
  }

  step : Box -> Box
  step (b) = b

  run : Box -> Integer
  run (b) = b.n + (step b).n

  opening : Integer = run (Box { n = 7 })
